      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BIRDY GAL (8) finished second two starts back at this track then gave nothing else a chance last start to win by 16 metres over 1609m at this track. Will need a bit of luck negotiating a very wide starting position. Meeting a deeper field this time but she has the ability to mix it with them. EXPLOSIVE BRONSKI (5) produced another strong performance last time when he battled on bravely to just miss out over 1609m at this track. Big chance based on that latest outing. RIO DE JANEIRO BLUE NZ (6) is worth another chance after a last-start seventh over 2125m at Penrith five days ago when racing wide for most of the trip when sent out as the favourite. SMOKESCREEN (10) was out of the money two runs ago then broke and finished ninth last start over 1609m at this track, coming home 22 metres from the winner. Will need a bit of luck negotiating a very wide starting position but is a live chance in a similar assignment.",
